$$

### Step 2: Calculate the total number of teachers
Each class has 3 teachers, and there are 40 classes.  
$$
\text{Total teachers} = 3 \text{ teachers/class} \times 40 \text{ classes} = 120 \text{ teachers}
$$

### Step 3: Calculate the number of trees planted by students
Each student plants 1 tree.  
$$
\text{Trees from students} = 1000 \text{ students} \times 1 \text{ tree/student} = 1000 \text{ trees}
$$

### Step 4: Calculate the number of trees planted by teachers
Each teacher plants 2 trees.  
$$
\text{Trees from teachers} = 120 \text{ teachers} \times 2 \text{ trees/teacher} = 240 \text{ trees}
$$

### Step 5: Add the total number of trees
$$
\text{Total trees planted} = 1000 \text{ trees (from students)} + 240 \text{ trees (from teachers)} = 1240 \text{ trees}
$$

Thus, the total number of trees that will be planted at the end of the campaign is:

$$
\boxed{1240}
$$

