$$

Next, we are informed that glue sticks come in packs of 8. To find out how many packs Mr. Jackson needs to buy, we divide the total number of glue sticks required by the number of glue sticks per pack:

$$
\frac{54}{8} = 6.75
$$

Since Mr. Jackson can only buy whole packs of glue sticks, we need to round up to the next whole number because even if there is a remainder, he can't purchase a fraction of a pack. Rounding 6.75 up gives us 7.

