Next, the true/false questions. There are 20 of them, each worth 1 point. She got 90% correct. So 90% of 20. That's 0.9 * 20 = 18. So she got 18 true/false questions right. Each is 1 point, so that's 18 * 1 = 18 points from true/false.

Now, the long-answer questions. There are 5 of them, each worth 5 points. She got 60% correct. So 60% of 5 is 0.6 * 5 = 3. So she got 3 long-answer questions correct. Each is worth 5 points, so that's 3 * 5 = 15 points from long-answer.

Now, adding all those up: 8 (multiple-choice) + 18 (true/false) + 15 (long-answer) = 41 points total.

